  {
    "id": "3467133405",
    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "Custom DELTARUNE Wallpaper",
    "description": "[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/13562353436708118945/D3DFD3020088BECF647D91B7CBDBD6966D027E7C/?imw=5000&imh=5000&ima=fit&impolicy=Letterbox&imcolor=%23000000&letterbox=false[/img]\n\nA highly customizable Deltarune-themed wallpaper.\n\n[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/16980005689832803108/B05605B29F39BD1991B8572289C9152B6877FECD/?imw=1024&imh=106&ima=fit&impolicy=Letterbox&imcolor=%23000000&letterbox=true[/img]\n\n- Rainbow Effect (With adjustable speed)\n- Clock (With 24h format support)\n- Deltarune Countdown (When a new chapter's release date gets announced, I will update the countdown to count down to the new date)\n- Rainbow Clock & Countdown\n- Wavy Effect\n- Custom Color (Can be set with \"Scheme color\")\n- Gloom Effect\n- The option to choose between 7 songs to play!\n- The ability to choose between 6 different scenes!\n\nSongs:\n- Before The Story\n- THE HOLY\n- WIth Hope Crossed on Our Hearts\n- Gallery\n- Another day in hometown\n- Castle Funk\n- Sunset of Seven Suns\n\nScenes:\n- Main Menu\n- Fountain Room\n- Fountain (Chapter 4)\n- Castle Town\n- River\n- Cliffs (Chapter 5)\n\n\n[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/11890368745441135779/B2700957EAB48C521CAE2B95066706662830FF20/?imw=1024&imh=106&ima=fit&impolicy=Letterbox&imcolor=%23000000&letterbox=true[/img]\n\nGloom & God Rays combined will cause sudden lighting flashes that could trigger photosensitive people. This can also occur when using God Rays & Rainbow together. There's not much I can do to counter this issue, all I ask is that you're careful when toggling those few features.\n\n[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/14155859126235773017/B5C2B5BAD5537E3B72F0F687273BAC88BEEED075/?imw=1024&imh=106&ima=fit&impolicy=Letterbox&imcolor=%23000000&letterbox=true[/img]\n\n- The Custom Color option breaks the Rainbow Effect. Keep that in mind.\n- The God Rays can be really bright when combined with the Gloom effect.\n- If a song stops playing, select another one and select the one you were playing to resume the song again. I'm working on fixing that.\n- You can set the theme to a shade of green (like #00ff5d) to fix the rainbow filter hiding some colors. I'm confused on how it works, but if it works it works.\n\n[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/9730496382892393283/6E98DEA71F283D0C92AFB1D0ED1F1ABB34D0E26B/?imw=1024&imh=106&ima=fit&impolicy=Letterbox&imcolor=%23000000&letterbox=true[/img]\n\nBackground by the Deltarune team (Extended by me)\nMusic by Toby Fox & Co.",
